If the API response is:
[
  {
    "id": 123,
    "name": "John"
  },
  {
    "id": 8646418,
    "name": "Bhuvanesh Khatri"
  }
]

What do we call each part?
- The entire response → JSON array
- Each { ... } inside the array → JSON object
- "id": 8646418 → key-value pair
- id → key/property
- 8646418 → value
- name → key/property
- "Bhuvanesh Khatri" → value
So:
JSON Response
     ↓
   Array
     ↓
 ┌───────────────┐
 │ JSON Object   │
 │ id: 123       │
 │ name: John    │
 └───────────────┘
     ↓
 ┌───────────────┐
 │ JSON Object   │
 │ id: 8646418   │
 │ name: Bhuvanesh│
 └───────────────┘

Therefore, in:
find{it.id==8646418}.name   // json Query Parameter

find{it.id==8646418}.name
│    │  │  │        │
│    │  │  │        └── Field to extract
│    │  │  └─────────── Value to compare
│    │  └────────────── Field being checked
│    └───────────────── Current object
└────────────────────── Search for matching object

it represents each JSON object currently being checked.